{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you shall do to him as he schemed.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said (Makkot 5a): From here — if they had him killed, they are not put to death, ״כַּאֲשֶׁר זָמַם״ — as he schemed, and not as he did. And it is difficult: perhaps the verse says ״כַּאֲשֶׁר זָמַם״ to render liable even if he did not carry it out, but rather from the moment he gave false testimony and schemed to do evil to his brother he became liable; and when the deed was carried out through him and [the accused] was killed, there is here both schemed and did, and I call that too זָמַם, with the addition that he also did — so is there not here the objection of אֵין עוֹנְשִׁין מִן הַדִּין (we do not punish by inference)?" "<b>Indeed,</b> the essence of the derashah is from the fact that it should have said ״כַּאֲשֶׁר עָנָה עַל אָחִיו״ — returning to what it stated, ״שֶׁקֶר עָנָה בְּאָחִיו״ — they shall do to him as he testified. And with this expression there would be liability whether [the accused] was killed or not killed, for both are included in the meaning of אֲשֶׁר עָנָה. And the fact that it did not use an inclusive expression but went and sought this expression ״אֲשֶׁר זָמַם״ — it comes for an inference, to say specifically זָמַם and not עָשָׂה, according to their words of blessed memory. And this is their language in the baraita (Makkot 5a): His father said to him, ״Is it not a fortiori?״ He said to him, ״You have taught us, our master, אֵין עוֹנְשִׁין מִן הַדִּין״ etc. One cannot raise a difficulty from this against their position, for even without the principle of ״אֵין עוֹנְשִׁין מִן הַדִּין,״ the a fortiori argument would have compelled us to say that the verse did not come to exempt them if they had him killed — for the matter is an a fortiori argument, and there is no force in an inference to override an a fortiori argument and to establish the verse other than by inference — were it not for the principle that Rabbi invoked, ״אֵין עוֹנְשִׁין מִן הַדִּין.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:13.114427109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}